# MANIFEST — Easy Kit
# One resource path per line (relative to the central clone root).
# Lines starting with # are comments. Blank lines are ignored.
# setup.sh reads this file and symlinks (or copies) each path into the target project.
#
# ── Optional destination column (T097 / DDR-0007) ────────────────────────────
# A line may carry trailing whitespace-separated `<harness>=<destination>` pairs:
#
#     <path>                <harness>=<dest-path>  [<harness>=<dest-path> ...]
#
# Field 1 is the ONLY field the base install reads — it copies each path to the
# same relative path in the target, exactly as before. A line with no trailing
# pairs therefore behaves identically to a pre-T097 MANIFEST, which is what makes
# `setup.sh` with no `--harness` flag byte-identical to the old install.
#
# The trailing pairs drive `setup.sh --harness <name>` / `update.sh --harness <name>`,
# which PROJECT field 1 into the named harness's own directory as real file copies.
# A harness with no pair on a line receives nothing for that path.
#
# `claude` deliberately appears in NO pair: `.claude/skills` and `.claude/agents`
# are relative SYMLINKS onto the plain-root canon (DDR-0007), installed by
# harness_install_canon_symlinks, not copies — a different mechanism, kept where
# it already lives rather than folded into the copy-projection loop.
#
# ── Exclusions (T113) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# A line `!<path>` keeps <path> — and everything under it — out of the project: it is
# not copied at install, not recorded in harness-lock.json, and not reported as a new
# file on update. It is a literal path prefix matched on whole path segments (no
# globs): `!.claude/hooks/tests` leaves `.claude/hooks/tests_helper.py` alone. A
# project's own file at an excluded path is never touched, backed up, or deleted.
# An exclusion is not an entry: every MANIFEST reader (installer, update, projection,
# scripts/validate.sh) must skip `!` lines when it reads paths or destinations.
#
# `agents` has no `codex=` pair on purpose: Codex 0.149.1 has no agent-guide
# directory it discovers, and DDR-0007/T097 forbid inventing one. Codex receives
# the kit's role doctrine through AGENTS.md instead.
#
# `packs` carries NO pair, and never may (ADR-0002, T116): it ships as a dormant
# Pack catalog that no CLI loads. A pack reaches a CLI only when the Supervisor
# activates it by copying it into agents/ and skills/.

# NOTE: .claude/settings.json is deployed by setup.sh as a per-project COPY
# (projects append their own permissions to it), not listed here.
agents
skills          codex=.codex/skills
.claude/hooks
templates
docs/claude-md
packs
AGENTS.md
.cursor/rules
!.claude/hooks/tests
